{"source":"E3","quote":"The entrepreneurship workshop was very helpful, and I learned a lot from the organizers, mentors, and other participants. We got to learn from experienced entrepreneurs and investors, and I got to pitch my business idea to a panel of judges. I received some valuable feedback and made some connections that could potentially lead to collaborations or investments.

I'm definitely considering applying to other startup accelerator programs or incubators in the future. In fact, I've been looking into a few options, and I think it could be a great way to take my business to the next level.

By the way, I've also been attending workshops on mindfulness and wellness, which I find helps me stay focused and calm when dealing with the stresses of entrepreneurship. I attended a half-day mindfulness workshop at a yoga studio near my home on December 12, and it was really helpful. I paid $20 to attend, and I got to take home a workbook with exercises and tips.","interpretation":"Paid $20 for a half-day mindfulness workshop on December 12","decision":"include"}
